## 9. Practical Learning Reflection

Week 2 helped me understand that building a chatbot is not only about writing responses or matching keywords.

A useful chatbot needs to understand what the user is trying to communicate, identify important information, handle different forms of language, and respond within clearly defined limits.

The activities also showed me that chatbot development involves both **technical considerations and ethical responsibility**.

In particular, testing with realistic language and relevant local examples can help identify situations where a chatbot may misunderstand a user's request.

